  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure is caused by **disk-full on the data filesystem** \u2014 not by permissions, container failure, or database.\n\n**Root cause: `/srv/lab-data` filesystem out of space**\n\n- Uploads fail in app code writing file: `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `out.write(chunk)` in `/app/main.py line 59` (E3).\n- `POST /upload` returned `200 OK` then started returning `500 Internal Server Error` at same time as that exception (E3).\n- Filesystem holding `/srv/lab-data` is its own mountpoint `mountpoint: /srv/lab-data` with `use_percent: 99.9`, `available_mb: 0.4`, `used_mb: 450.9 / size_mb: 487.2` (E4).\n- Inodes are not exhausted: `inode_use_percent: 0.3` (E4), so this is block-capacity exhaustion.\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n- Root filesystem is healthy: `use_percent: 6.8`, `available_mb: 91424.1` on `/` (E5) \u2014 problem is isolated to `/srv/lab-data`.\n- Permissions: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir: true`, `owner_uid: 1000`, `app_uid: 1000`, `app_user_can_write: true` (E6).\n- Mount / user: app is `running`, `user: 1000:1000`, `mounts: bind source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw: true` (E7) \u2014 mount is present and writable.\n- Database dependency is healthy: `database system is ready to accept connections` (E8), `health: healthy`, `running: true`, `oom_killed: false` (E10), `health_status: healthy` for `incidentlab-db-1` (E9).\n- App container itself is `running` (E1)(E7) and `/health` returns `status_code: 200 body: {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2) \u2014 failure is specific to upload writes, health check does not catch storage full.\n- No crash/OOM: `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false`, `restart_count: 0` for app (E7) and db (E10); recent `die exit_code: 0` were clean stops/recreates (E9).\n\nConclusion: uploads stopped because writes to the bind-mounted `/srv/lab-data` cannot allocate blocks. Symptom is `500` on `POST /upload` (E3); health `200` (E2) is misleading.\n",
